NAME
    cpu - run a command on another machine

SYNOPSIS
    cpu <host:port> <command...>

DESCRIPTION
    Runs <command> on the machine at host:port using its /bin, but reading THIS
    machine's files through the namespace imported at /host. Within the
    command, / is the remote and /host is you. The Plan 9 cpu model.

EXAMPLES
    cpu 10.0.2.10:564 ls /host
    cpu 10.0.2.10:564 cat /host/notes.txt

SEE ALSO
    mount, dial
